WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.958 --> 00:00:32.500
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna explained</b>

2
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:38.291
<b>that to conquer desire, one must</b>
<b>begin with controlling the senses. </b>

3
00:00:38.291 --> 00:00:41.416
<b>This is because senses are tangible;</b>

4
00:00:41.416 --> 00:00:45.958
<b>their experience can be felt and understood.</b>

5
00:00:45.958 --> 00:00:49.583
<b>However, senses are not supreme.</b>

6
00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:54.375
<b>In this verse, Krishna elaborates on this concept,</b>

7
00:00:54.375 --> 00:01:04.500
<b>explaining the hierarchy of soul, intellect, </b>
<b>mind, senses, body, and material objects.</b>

8
00:01:09.208 --> 00:01:10.791
<b>This verse states</b>

9
00:01:10.791 --> 00:01:13.375
<b>that the senses are superior to the body,</b>

10
00:01:13.375 --> 00:01:15.750
<b>the mind is superior to the senses,</b>

11
00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.166
<b>the intellect is superior to the mind,</b>

12
00:01:18.166 --> 00:01:22.333
<b>and ultimately, the soul is superior to the intellect.</b>

13
00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:28.375
<b>Any contact with material </b>
<b>objects requires a body.</b>

14
00:01:28.375 --> 00:01:30.000
<b>For instance,</b>

15
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.708
<b>can a piece of ice give you </b>
<b>the sensation of cold by itself?</b>

16
00:01:35.708 --> 00:01:36.791
<b>No.</b>

17
00:01:36.791 --> 00:01:44.333
<b>You must touch it, which isn't </b>
<b>possible against the body's will.</b>

18
00:01:44.333 --> 00:01:47.500
<b>So here, the ice is helpless;</b>

19
00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:49.791
<b>the body is superior.</b>

20
00:01:49.791 --> 00:01:51.500
<b>Now understand this hierarchy:</b>

21
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:57.541
<b>if the mind decides the body should remain still, </b>
<b>the body is powerless.</b>

22
00:01:57.541 --> 00:02:00.208
<b>Thus, the mind is superior to the body.</b>

23
00:02:00.208 --> 00:02:01.291
<b>Similarly,</b>

24
00:02:01.291 --> 00:02:04.750
<b>if the intellect determines what it wants to do,</b>

25
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:07.208
<b>then the mind will remain in control.</b>

26
00:02:07.208 --> 00:02:09.166
<b>So intellect is superior to mind.</b>

27
00:02:09.166 --> 00:02:11.000
<b>And finally, the soul.</b>

28
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.666
<b>The soul is the source of consciousness,</b>

29
00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.583
<b>superior even to intellect,</b>

30
00:02:15.583 --> 00:02:21.458
<b>because only a conscious being can use intellect.</b>

31
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:27.958
<b>and as the level increases, </b>
<b>control becomes more complex,</b>

32
00:02:27.958 --> 00:02:36.666
<b>which is why the simplest way to</b>
<b>control desire is to regulate sensory contact.</b>

33
00:02:36.666 --> 00:02:39.083
<b>The relationship between these elements </b>

34
00:02:39.083 --> 00:02:42.625
<b>can be understood through </b>
<b>the metaphor of a chariot:</b>

35
00:02:42.625 --> 00:02:43.833
<b>in which, </b>

36
00:02:43.833 --> 00:02:46.916
<b>The chariot's passenger – is the soul.</b>

37
00:02:46.916 --> 00:02:50.125
<b>The charioteer – is the intellect.</b>

38
00:02:50.125 --> 00:02:53.500
<b>The horses – are the 5 senses</b>

39
00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.333
<b>eyes,</b>

40
00:02:54.333 --> 00:02:55.208
<b>ears,</b>

41
00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.166
<b>skin,</b>

42
00:02:56.166 --> 00:02:57.083
<b>tongue,</b>

43
00:02:57.083 --> 00:02:58.333
<b>nose</b>

44
00:02:58.333 --> 00:03:01.416
<b>The reins of these horses – is the mind.</b>

45
00:03:01.416 --> 00:03:04.000
<b>And the chariot – is the body</b>

46
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.833
<b>Understand it this way:</b>

47
00:03:05.833 --> 00:03:10.791
<b>the passenger gives directions to the charioteer,</b>

48
00:03:10.791 --> 00:03:20.750
<b>and according to these instructions, the </b>
<b>charioteer controls the horses through the reins,</b>

49
00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.916
<b>resulting in the chariot's movement.</b>

50
00:03:23.916 --> 00:03:25.083
<b>Similarly,</b>

51
00:03:25.083 --> 00:03:30.666
<b>the soul-passenger directs </b>
<b>its charioteer-intellect,</b>

52
00:03:30.666 --> 00:03:39.250
<b>and then the intellect controls the </b>
<b>five sense-horses through the mind-reins,</b>

53
00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:44.666
<b>and through this sequence, </b>
<b>action occurs in the body-chariot.</b>

54
00:03:44.666 --> 00:03:45.625
<b>In this scenario,</b>

55
00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:49.000
<b>if the passenger—the soul—is confused,</b>

56
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.375
<b>no progress will occur.</b>

57
00:03:51.375 --> 00:03:54.958
<b>The charioteer won't be able to control the reins,</b>

58
00:03:54.958 --> 00:04:01.375
<b>and consequently, the sense-horses </b>
<b>will try to go in different directions,</b>

59
00:04:01.375 --> 00:04:06.791
<b>resulting only in chaos and disorder.</b>

60
00:04:06.791 --> 00:04:13.583
<b>Most people live at the lower level, that is, </b>
<b>at the level of senses and objects—</b>

61
00:04:13.583 --> 00:04:16.208
<b>a life of mere pleasure.</b>

62
00:04:16.208 --> 00:04:20.375
<b>Some thoughtful people reach the mind level,</b>

63
00:04:20.375 --> 00:04:26.000
<b>where they somewhat recognize</b>
<b>their thoughts and emotions.</b>

64
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.500
<b>Some reach the level of intellect where </b>
<b>they can distinguish between beneficial </b>

65
00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.250
<b>and harmful thoughts.</b>

66
00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:39.750
<b>At the highest position are those who </b>
<b>understand their spiritual nature</b>

67
00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:46.416
<b>and believe that the soul </b>
<b>animates all lower levels.</b>

68
00:04:51.125 --> 00:04:57.083
<b>Reflect on your daily routine.</b>

69
00:04:57.083 --> 00:05:01.791
<b>Countless times each day, unknowingly,</b>

70
00:05:01.791 --> 00:05:09.333
<b>you react naturally to </b>
<b>what you see, hear, or touch.</b>

71
00:05:09.333 --> 00:05:16.333
<b>These uncontrolled reactions </b>
<b>are triggered by your senses,</b>

72
00:05:16.333 --> 00:05:23.791
<b>which are constantly in contact </b>
<b>with the world around them.</b>

73
00:05:23.791 --> 00:05:25.125
<b>Although</b>

74
00:05:25.125 --> 00:05:31.791
<b>these senses help us experience the </b>
<b>tangible aspects of this world,</b>

75
00:05:31.791 --> 00:05:42.125
<b>these five senses are merely the smallest </b>
<b>part of our greater consciousness system.</b>

76
00:05:42.125 --> 00:05:44.583
<b>In explaining this verse,</b>

77
00:05:44.583 --> 00:05:48.958
<b>the beautiful metaphor of a chariot</b>

78
00:05:48.958 --> 00:05:58.083
<b>illustrates the relationship between</b>
<b>body, senses, mind, intellect, and soul.</b>

79
00:05:58.083 --> 00:06:05.000
<b>Can we apply this understanding </b>
<b>to our daily lives?</b>

80
00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.541
<b>Most certainly.</b>

81
00:06:07.541 --> 00:06:12.625
<b>It begins by recognizing</b>

82
00:06:12.625 --> 00:06:24.958
<b>that fulfilling every desire of the senses </b>
<b>is like letting horses run without control.</b>

83
00:06:24.958 --> 00:06:27.166
<b>If this happens,</b>

84
00:06:27.166 --> 00:06:37.666
<b>they might lead us to places that</b>
<b>are inappropriate or harmful.</b>

85
00:06:37.666 --> 00:06:39.416
<b>Therefore,</b>

86
00:06:39.416 --> 00:06:47.875
<b>we must control these sense-horses </b>
<b>using the reins of our mind.</b>

87
00:06:47.875 --> 00:06:49.083
<b>But</b>

88
00:06:49.083 --> 00:06:51.000
<b>consider this:</b>

89
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:57.416
<b>what use are reins tied to the horses</b>

90
00:06:57.416 --> 00:07:09.166
<b>if there's no charioteer to control that mind? </b>
<b>Without this, all is futile.</b>

91
00:07:09.166 --> 00:07:15.583
<b>This is why we must develop our intellect</b>

92
00:07:15.583 --> 00:07:20.333
<b>so it can hold the reins of the mind.</b>

93
00:07:20.333 --> 00:07:26.166
<b>Choose only the direction that </b>
<b>aligns with our life values.</b>

94
00:07:26.166 --> 00:07:28.583
<b>And ultimately,</b>

95
00:07:28.583 --> 00:07:37.000
<b>this charioteer-like intellect will receive </b>
<b>direction from the soul-like passenger.</b>

96
00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:46.250
<b>Whether life values are good or bad </b>
<b>directly relates to our spiritual level.</b>

97
00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:50.125
<b>And from here, the entire process</b>

98
00:07:50.125 --> 00:07:56.666
<b>will either be controlled or spiral into chaos.</b>

99
00:07:56.666 --> 00:08:03.583
<b>Understand that the soul's level </b>
<b>alone will determine</b>

100
00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:10.458
<b>whether we're progressing toward </b>
<b>elevation or degradation.</b>

101
00:08:10.458 --> 00:08:13.041
<b>The essence of this verse is that</b>

102
00:08:13.041 --> 00:08:20.958
<b>we shouldn't limit our thinking to </b>
<b>just tangible objects and sensations.</b>

103
00:08:20.958 --> 00:08:23.416
<b>We must expand this thinking</b>

104
00:08:23.416 --> 00:08:32.916
<b>and strive to know and </b>
<b>develop our true spiritual level.</b>

105
00:08:32.916 --> 00:08:34.291
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

106
00:08:39.041 --> 00:08:41.500
<b>Just as this verse</b>

107
00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:53.083
<b>explains how senses, mind, intellect, </b>
<b>and soul operate at different levels,</b>

108
00:08:53.083 --> 00:08:54.375
<b>similarly,</b>

109
00:08:54.375 --> 00:09:04.000
<b>family members function at different levels of</b>
<b>understanding and spiritual consciousness.</b>

110
00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:11.625
<b>Encouraging each person toward the </b>
<b>right yoga according to their present state,</b>

111
00:09:11.625 --> 00:09:18.916
<b>and ultimately engaging them in that yoga, </b>
<b>can be tremendously helpful.</b>

112
00:09:18.916 --> 00:09:27.666
<b>For family members who are more inclined</b>
<b>toward physical activities and tangible results,</b>

113
00:09:27.666 --> 00:09:29.750
<b>for them, </b>

114
00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:34.541
<b>Karma Yoga can be a good beginning.</b>

115
00:09:34.541 --> 00:09:38.416
<b>This yoga promotes selfless action</b>

116
00:09:38.416 --> 00:09:44.458
<b>and provides a practical path for </b>
<b>family members, especially youth,</b>

117
00:09:44.458 --> 00:09:54.750
<b>to learn the importance of service and acting </b>
<b>without attachment to results.</b>

118
00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:57.166
<b>For those family members</b>

119
00:09:57.166 --> 00:10:02.625
<b>who are more inclined toward </b>
<b>knowledge and contemplation,</b>

120
00:10:02.625 --> 00:10:04.250
<b>for them,</b>

121
00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:08.166
<b>Gyan Yoga might be more appealing.</b>

122
00:10:08.166 --> 00:10:11.458
<b>This is the path of knowledge and intellect.</b>

123
00:10:11.458 --> 00:10:15.500
<b>It can include deep study of philosophical texts</b>

124
00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:21.083
<b>and collective discussions </b>
<b>on life's bigger questions.</b>

125
00:10:21.083 --> 00:10:22.000
<b>Meanwhile,</b>

126
00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:32.208
<b>for members already progressing on the path</b>
<b>of personal and spiritual development,</b>

127
00:10:32.208 --> 00:10:35.833
<b>Dhyana Yoga can be beneficial.</b>

128
00:10:35.833 --> 00:10:44.375
<b>This practice helps develop deep </b>
<b>self-awareness and discipline.</b>

129
00:10:44.375 --> 00:10:54.583
<b>And for those who wish to establish a direct </b>
<b>emotional and devotional connection with God,</b>

130
00:10:54.583 --> 00:10:56.375
<b>there is</b>

131
00:10:56.375 --> 00:11:01.250
<b>Bhakti Yoga—the path of devotion.</b>

132
00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:05.291
<b>This may include singing devotional </b>
<b>songs together as a family,</b>

133
00:11:05.291 --> 00:11:07.833
<b>participating in religious ceremonies,</b>

134
00:11:07.833 --> 00:11:14.750
<b>or praying regularly as a family unit.</b>

135
00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:21.958
<b>Such collective activities can</b>
<b>deepen family emotional bonds</b>

136
00:11:21.958 --> 00:11:29.166
<b>and connect everyone at a </b>
<b>profound spiritual level.</b>

137
00:11:29.166 --> 00:11:30.541
<b>For everyone,</b>

138
00:11:30.541 --> 00:11:36.250
<b>there exists a yoga according </b>
<b>to their level and interest.</b>

139
00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:40.875
<b>In this path of yoga, motivating family members,</b>

140
00:11:40.875 --> 00:11:46.625
<b>not merely for those members, </b>
<b>but for the whole family,</b>

141
00:11:46.625 --> 00:11:52.083
<b>can become a pathway to spiritual elevation.</b>

142
00:11:52.083 --> 00:11:54.250
<b>Consider this.</b>

143
00:11:58.916 --> 00:12:03.708
<b>Think about today's workplaces,</b>

144
00:12:03.708 --> 00:12:06.333
<b>where continuous activities,</b>

145
00:12:06.333 --> 00:12:08.750
<b>different types of work,</b>

146
00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:11.083
<b>various people,</b>

147
00:12:11.083 --> 00:12:12.750
<b>interactions,</b>

148
00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:17.541
<b>and countless things occur simultaneously.</b>

149
00:12:17.541 --> 00:12:25.250
<b>All this keeps our senses constantly </b>
<b>engaged in some form.</b>

150
00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:29.583
<b>Our senses absorb these experiences,</b>

151
00:12:29.583 --> 00:12:37.708
<b>which affect our mind, our intellect,</b>
<b>and ultimately our soul.</b>

152
00:12:37.708 --> 00:12:42.250
<b>Understanding and controlling these influences</b>

153
00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:53.250
<b>can help not only in increasing our work efficiency </b>
<b>but also in making that work more fulfilling.</b>

154
00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:55.500
<b>For instance,</b>

155
00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:56.791
<b>during work,</b>

156
00:12:56.791 --> 00:13:00.583
<b>eavesdropping on others' conversations,</b>

157
00:13:00.583 --> 00:13:04.833
<b>the urge to chat with a friend on the phone,</b>

158
00:13:04.833 --> 00:13:07.166
<b>the attraction to see something new,</b>

159
00:13:07.166 --> 00:13:13.333
<b>or such distractions that divert us from our work</b>

160
00:13:13.333 --> 00:13:17.458
<b>all arise through the senses.</b>

161
00:13:17.458 --> 00:13:22.083
<b>The mind processes signals </b>
<b>received through the senses,</b>

162
00:13:22.083 --> 00:13:28.666
<b>and guided by intellect, either transforms </b>
<b>these signals into intense desires</b>

163
00:13:28.666 --> 00:13:34.208
<b>or can control them through proper reasoning.</b>

164
00:13:34.208 --> 00:13:38.333
<b>If we want to reduce these attractions</b>

165
00:13:38.333 --> 00:13:43.708
<b>and focus completely on work,</b>

166
00:13:43.708 --> 00:13:49.708
<b>it must begin with controlling the </b>
<b>signals received by the senses.</b>

167
00:13:49.708 --> 00:13:52.875
<b>It starts with their control.</b>

168
00:13:52.875 --> 00:13:56.041
<b>If these signals themselves decrease,</b>

169
00:13:56.041 --> 00:13:59.750
<b>control becomes much easier.</b>

170
00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:01.208
<b>For example,</b>

171
00:14:01.208 --> 00:14:08.833
<b>not checking personal phones during </b>
<b>important work, keeping them silent.</b>

172
00:14:08.833 --> 00:14:12.041
<b>This will reduce distractions.</b>

173
00:14:12.041 --> 00:14:20.166
<b>But sensory signals cannot </b>
<b>be completely eliminated.</b>

174
00:14:20.166 --> 00:14:28.458
<b>So the next level is mind control, so that</b>
<b>even if senses receive signals,</b>

175
00:14:28.458 --> 00:14:31.416
<b>they don't have an impact.</b>

176
00:14:31.416 --> 00:14:40.916
<b>To keep the mind focused, even for just a few </b>
<b>moments in the morning at home or workplace,</b>

177
00:14:40.916 --> 00:14:46.000
<b>practicing meditation and spiritual </b>
<b>discipline, can be helpful.</b>

178
00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:49.041
<b>Above the mind is the level of intellect,</b>

179
00:14:49.041 --> 00:14:52.875
<b>which shapes our decision-making process,</b>

180
00:14:52.875 --> 00:14:57.500
<b>considers aspects of morality and immorality.</b>

181
00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:04.708
<b>And to strengthen intellect, </b>
<b>continuous learning, constant study,</b>

182
00:15:04.708 --> 00:15:06.625
<b>and above all,</b>

183
00:15:06.625 --> 00:15:09.541
<b>self-reflection are helpful.</b>

184
00:15:09.541 --> 00:15:16.333
<b>This improves not just work skills, </b>
<b>but also our moral character.</b>

185
00:15:16.333 --> 00:15:20.208
<b>And at the highest level is the soul,</b>

186
00:15:20.208 --> 00:15:22.458
<b>which is the foundation of our consciousness,</b>

187
00:15:22.458 --> 00:15:27.958
<b>and controls intellect, mind, and senses.</b>

188
00:15:27.958 --> 00:15:32.250
<b>It's essential to keep elevating our spiritual level.</b>

189
00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:37.000
<b>This teaches us that no work is purely individual,</b>

190
00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:42.291
<b>as its good or bad effects impact others too.</b>

191
00:15:42.291 --> 00:15:45.833
<b>This lifts us above selfishness,</b>

192
00:15:45.833 --> 00:15:48.250
<b>makes us more aware, and</b>

193
00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:57.166
<b>inspires us to think about how our </b>
<b>work benefits others in society.</b>

194
00:15:57.166 --> 00:15:58.666
<b>Consider this!</b>

195
00:15:58.666 --> 00:16:05.208
<b>When you begin to believe that your </b>
<b>work isn't just for personal gain,</b>

196
00:16:05.208 --> 00:16:08.750
<b>but rather a contribution to society.</b>

197
00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:13.333
<b>Then with this perspective, </b>
<b>how magnificent every task will seem,</b>

198
00:16:13.333 --> 00:16:16.916
<b>how satisfying it will become.</b>

199
00:16:16.916 --> 00:16:19.291
<b>How beautiful is this vision!</b>

